From: OnePlus 15 recovery maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] startup: respect current vold ownership of keystore sync

The current vold API removed copySqliteDb. It already synchronizes the tmpfs
database inside Decrypt_User_Synth_Pass before looking up synthetic-password
keys. Leave that backend unchanged and remove only the obsolete startup call.
The device patch runner verifies the replacement API and ownership first.

diff --git a/twrp.cpp b/twrp.cpp
--- a/twrp.cpp
+++ b/twrp.cpp
@@ -225,4 +225,3 @@
-#ifdef TW_INCLUDE_CRYPTO
-	android::keystore::copySqliteDb();
-#endif
+	// Current vold synchronizes its tmpfs keystore database inside Decrypt_User_Synth_Pass.
+	// Do not call the removed pre-decrypt copySqliteDb startup API.
 	Decrypt_Page(skip_decryption, datamedia);
